STEP 1 -- THE BRANCH TABLES OBEY TWO MACHINE-INDEPENDENT RECURRENCES
------------------------------------------------------------------------
  A_(v+2) = 3A_(v+1) - 2A_v   and   B_(v+3) = 4B_(v+2) - 5B_(v+1) + 2B_v
  4000 random machines x 40 branches: 0 violations
  (characteristic polynomials (X-2)(X-1) and (X-2)(X-1)^2 -- the whole
   family lies on one 5-dimensional solution space)

STEP 2 -- THEOREM R: rigid <=> v_2(B_v) < v_2(A_v)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
  6462 (machine, branch) pairs, k <= 899: 0 disagreements

STEP 3 -- T13: how much of the family is provably computation-free
------------------------------------------------------------------------
  well-defined machines in the box: 19092
  globally rigid (direct check, v < 200): 2351  (12.31%)
  all of them have beta even: True
  criterion exact on beta even and NONZERO (8716 machines): True (1593 rigid)
  beta = 0 (1537 machines): 758 rigid -- the case the criterion omits
    e.g. (1,0,1,1,0): v_2(A_v) for v = 0..5 is [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6] -> unbounded, so
    rigidity is generic there, not exceptional

STEP 4 -- THE COUNTING BARRIER IS REFUTED: bandwidth is at least M
------------------------------------------------------------------------
  M = 23   best bandwidth over 400 random machines: 100    >= M: True
  M = 101  best bandwidth over 400 random machines: 412    >= M: True
  M = 257  best bandwidth over 400 random machines: 1036   >= M: True
  A Conway-style reduction mod M needs M independent branch pieces.
  VAL(2) supplies at least that many -- so periodicity, while true,
  yields a structure theorem and NOT an impossibility.

STEP 5 -- WHAT SURVIVES: the slope-resolution bound (every machine)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
  #{v : |s_v - alpha| >= rho} = floor(log2(|beta|/rho))
  9000 (machine, rho) pairs: 0 mismatches
  => k branches pairwise rho-separated in slope cost |beta| >= rho*2^(k-1):
     an EXPONENTIAL compression bound, not an impossibility.

========================================================================
RESULT: R and T13 proved; the counting barrier is refuted, and the
reason retires the genre -- universality is a property of a single
point, not of a family. VAL(2) universality remains OPEN.
